<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yin Shan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yin Shan are a range of mountains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>, north of the great bend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>. They formed a frontier zone between the Chinese plains and the steppe. In 682 CE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilterish-qaghan">Ilterish Qaghan</a> began to rebuild Turkic power with a handful of followers in the Yin Shan, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-turkic-khaganate">Second Turkic Khaganate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yin-shan.jpg" alt="Yin Shan" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: wanghongliu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%91%BC%E5%92%8C%E6%B5%A9%E7%89%B9%E5%8C%97%E9%9D%A2%E7%9A%84%E5%A4%A7%E9%9D%92%E5%B1%B1(%E9%98%B4%E5%B1%B1%E5%B1%B1%E8%84%89)_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
